{"name":"Swag Bag Silver","hex":"#b1b8b5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"swag","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To (cause to) sway.","To droop; to sag."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A loop of draped fabric.","Something that droops like a swag."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swag"},{"term":"bag","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tuki."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft container made out of cloth, paper, thin plastic, etc. and open at the top, used to hold food, commodities, and other goods.","A container made of leather, plastic, or other material, usually with a handle or handles, in which you carry personal items, or clothes or other things that you need for travelling. Includes shopping bags, schoolbags, suitcases, briefcases, handbags, backpacks, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bag"},{"term":"silver","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lustrous, white, metallic element, atomic number 47, atomic weight 107.87, symbol Ag.","Coins made from silver or any similar white metal."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from silver.","Made from another white metal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver"}],"entries":[{"title":"Promotional merchandise","blocks":[{"text":"Promotional merchandise are products branded with a logo or slogan and distributed at little or no cost to promote a brand, corporate identity, or event. Such products, which are often informally called promo products, swag, or freebies, are used in marketing and sales. Often they are of the tchotchke type. They are given away or sold at a loss to promote a company, corporate image, brand, or event. They are often distributed as handouts at trade shows, at conferences, on sales calls, and as bonus items in shipped orders. They are often used in guerrilla marketing campaigns. Ones for video games are often called feelies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Vintage_RCA_Promotional_Items%2C_RCA_Plant%2C_Lancaster%2C_Pennsylvania_%2810007796245%29.jpg/330px-Vintage_RCA_Promotional_Items%2C_RCA_Plant%2C_Lancaster%2C_Pennsylvania_%2810007796245%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Promotional_merchandise"},{"title":"Bag","blocks":[{"text":"A bag, also known regionally as a sack or tote, is a common tool in the form of a floppy container, typically made of cloth, leather, bamboo, paper, or plastic. The use of bags predates recorded history, with the earliest bags being lengths of animal skin, cotton, or woven plant fibers, folded up at the edges and secured in that shape with strings of the same material. Bags can be used to carry items such as personal belongings, groceries, tools, and other objects. They come in various shapes and sizes, often equipped with handles or straps for easier carrying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Bolsas-de-asa-plana-interior-bolsapubli.jpg/330px-Bolsas-de-asa-plana-interior-bolsapubli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bag"},{"title":"Silver","blocks":[{"text":"Silver is a chemical element; it has symbol Ag and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity and reflectivity of any metal. Silver is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form, as an alloy with gold (electrum) and other metals, and in minerals such as acanthite, argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is recovered as a byproduct of lead–zinc, copper and gold mining and refining."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Silver_crystal.jpg/330px-Silver_crystal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver"},{"title":"Silver (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver or metallic gray is a color tone resembling gray that is a representation of the color of polished silver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png/330px-Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/SwissParkingDisk.jpg/500px-SwissParkingDisk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/SwissParkingDisk.jpg/1280px-SwissParkingDisk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/SwissParkingDisk.jpg/500px-SwissParkingDisk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Swiss parking disk (early 1970s). Selected arrival time shows at the left window, departure at the right. Other side of disk is used for afternoon parking. Disk was a sales promotion for UBS bank.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwissParkingDisk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Dharma_Girl_%282713333430%29.jpg/500px-Dharma_Girl_%282713333430%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Dharma_Girl_%282713333430%29.jpg/1280px-Dharma_Girl_%282713333430%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Dharma_Girl_%282713333430%29.jpg/500px-Dharma_Girl_%282713333430%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A woman dressed as a member of the ficti